# MMMTAP P1-022 — back to the thesis

**Status:** Protocol and offline corpus inventory only. **Not** an executable model-calling harness. No hosted calls, credentials, Azure resources or security-action automation.

Read `PREREGISTRATION.md` in full. It separates verified historical evidence, forward-frozen discovery material, adjudication, correction arms and regression checks. The historic corpus has already featured in MMMTAP and must not be described as untouched.

### On Gaia

```bash
cd ~/git
unzip -t ~/mmmtap_p1_022.zip || exit 1
unzip -n ~/mmmtap_p1_022.zip || exit 1
python3 -m py_compile mmmtap_p1_022/inventory.py
python3 mmmtap_p1_022/inventory.py \
  --source ~/mmmtap_p1_014_verified_inputs.zip \
  --out ~/git/mmmtap_p1_022/p1_022_inventory.json
```

If your original archive is elsewhere, set `--source` to its **existing** location. This only audits 15×9 corpus members, checks recovery metadata and writes a reproducible five/ten case partition. Source ZIP untouched.

**Next stage gate:** Inspect actual Phase 0 code contracts and historical labels, obtain independent adjudication rubric and freeze execution prompts before implementing/starting a call. We should not burn inference credits yet. If no independently verified susceptible cases exist, report that and run only a separate regression-introduction test.

### Portability fix (v0.1.1)
The packaged frozen inventory records the author's local absolute source path. `inventory.py` now ignores only that location when comparing an existing inventory. The source ZIP SHA-256, all 135 input hashes, counts, partition and all other metadata remain strict. It never overwrites the frozen inventory.
